    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1389">

                <pb facs="1357" n="1347" xml:id="pg1347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.0015/9–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-23T16:00:00+08:00">September 23,
                            1949—4 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 23—5:44 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4008. Re Cantel 1142, sent Shanghai 545. APL Shanghai informs Consulate General
                    no holders Chinese passports booked on <hi rendition="#italic">Gordon</hi>, but
                    have booked approximately 20 persons Chinese birth who hold foreign passports or
                    IRO stateless travel documents in lieu passports.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated Canton 1128, Taipei 306, Hong Kong 269.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
